/home/user/sdk-alif/optional/modules/lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/docs/online_memory_allocation_overview.md-28-
/home/user/sdk-alif/optional/modules/lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/docs/online_memory_allocation_overview.md-29-The TFLite flatbuffer model contains a variety of information required to run a
/home/user/sdk-alif/optional/modules/lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/docs/online_memory_allocation_overview.md-30-model in TFLite or TFLM. The TFLM online memory planner will walk the main
/home/user/sdk-alif/optional/modules/lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/docs/online_memory_allocation_overview.md-31-subgraph and find all tensors required for the model (represented as
/home/user/sdk-alif/optional/modules/lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/docs/online_memory_allocation_overview.md:32:`TfLiteTensor` and `TfLiteEvalTensor` C structs at runtime). Persistent tensors
/home/user/sdk-alif/optional/modules/lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/docs/online_memory_allocation_overview.md-33-in the flatbuffer (e.g. weight tensors) will point at a buffer inlined in the
